WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
A demonstration with drawn screens: the setup page, then the dashboard.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.500
In a terminal, install.sh --wizard opens the setup page on your computer.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.000
The first screen says what it found in your folder and proposes a way to work.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.500
Install the kit: its files go beside your code. Nothing is committed or pushed.

5
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.000
Confirm the rules, then register a second identity that reviews every change.

6
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Publish sends the kit to main. Your idea and plan wait for your approval.

7
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Write your idea in one line. Your coding agent drafts the plan.

8
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.500
Each task lists the checks it must pass. You approve by typing the folder's name.

9
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:40.500
Start this agent opens a terminal with it; below it, the same command to copy.

10
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.500
Each task claims its files, so two agents never edit the same one.

11
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:49.000
The last screen follows the project, and your app's link once it is deployed.

12
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.000
The dashboard shows every task as a square: integrated, in review, in progress or waiting.

13
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Point at a square to see what it waits for and what it unblocks.

14
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.000
What waits for you comes first. An approved change merges once the checks pass.

15
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.000
Agents: one card each, with its task and when it was last seen.

16
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.500
Edit arranges the summary: move, hide or add blocks.

17
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.000
Share turns the progress into an image to post.
